.TH AVR\-FIREWALL\-EDIT 1 "" "avr 0.7.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-firewall-edit \- Edit specified fields of an existing firewall rule.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr firewall edit
[OPTIONS] RULE_ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edit specified fields of an existing firewall rule.
.PP
Edit only the supplied fields, preserving rule identity and order. Switching hostname/CIDR clears the other matcher. Any or ICMP clears ports. Use --ports all to remove a port restriction; numeric ports require a TCP/UDP rule.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIRULE_ID\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fICHOICE\fR
(choices: allow, deny)
.TP
\fB\-\-proto\fR \fICHOICE\fR
(choices: tcp, udp, icmp, any)
.TP
\fB\-\-cidr\fR \fITEXT\fR
Destination IPv4 address or CIDR; replaces the hostname.
.TP
\fB\-\-fqdn\fR \fITEXT\fR
Destination hostname; replaces the CIDR.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug; defaults to the configured organization.
.TP
\fB\-\-ports\fR \fITEXT\fR
Port, range, or all to clear the port restriction.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository ID or owner/repo. If provided, uses repository scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-firewall (1),
.BR avr-firewall-add (1),
.BR avr-firewall-delete (1),
.BR avr-firewall-export (1),
.BR avr-firewall-flow-summaries (1),
.BR avr-firewall-import (1),
